CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:Márgenes is a festival dedicated to contemporary cinema\, wit
 h a particular focus on innovative works that bring together emerging and 
 established talent. Its programme explores the convergence between cinema
 \, the visual arts\, and sound art\, featuring screenings\, audiovisual pe
 rformances\, talks\, and family-friendly sessions\, thereby expanding the 
 boundaries of the cinematic experience.International filmmakers of the cal
 ibre of Leos Carax\, Lucien Castaing-Taylor\, Mariano Llinás\, Radu Jude
 \, and Quentin Dupieux appear alongside Spanish directors such as Eloy Enc
 iso\, Meritxell Colell\, María Molina Peiró\, Natalia Marín\, and Helen
 a Girón & Samuel Delgado\, as well as sound and visual artists includi\nC
 ategory: Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.o
 rg/en/schedule/margenes-2026
LOCATION:Sala Azcona\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/margenes-2026
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
